  "description": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "<p>Fisher College is a private college situated in Boston, Massachusetts. Fisher College welcomes international students from all over the world to the university. Founded in 1903, Fisher College is one of the leading bachelorâ€™s and masterâ€™s degree-granting institutions in Boston.</p><h2>What is the Fisher College, Boston acceptance rate for International Students?</h2><p>The Fisher College, Boston acceptance rate is 69%.</p> <p>The Department of Information Services provides the college with computer laboratories, technical training, network support, and more so students can make the most of technological innovation. Science laboratories are also located on campus for students to utilize.</p><p>The fitness center and gymnasium are two other fitness spaces where students can benefit from healthy exercise. The Fisher cafe is the main food outlet on campus, but there are other dietary preferences for students to choose from.</p> <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p> <p>Campus life provides many opportunities for students to socialize together and lead a well-balanced life. From yoga club to becoming a part of the student center and beyond, students can pursue their interests and make friends alongside their studies. Volunteering opportunities around campus help all students to feel a part of the community as they lead the change in making a difference. Students often meet over breakfast or dinner in the Dining Hall, with a range of hot food, deli sandwiches and more treats on offer to students and staff.</p>"
    ],
